WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.043 --> 00:00:10.967
Recently, many stores have started to offer organic food products, meaning those that are grown or made without

2
00:00:11.007 --> 00:00:12.548
the use of artificial chemicals.

3
00:00:13.369 --> 00:00:19.833
Although organic farmers do use fertilizers and pesticides on their crops, the chemicals are natural and used in

4
00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:20.693
lower quantities.

5
00:00:21.414 --> 00:00:26.817
As a result, organic methods produce foods that are healthier for the environment and for humans.

6
00:00:27.518 --> 00:00:34.321
Even though organic foods have only recently become popular, growing crops organically is not a modern development; organic

7
00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:37.202
farming is the oldest kind of agriculture in the world.

8
00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:44.084
Natural chemicals have been used by farmers to produce food for thousands of years, whereas artificial chemicals were

9
00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:46.685
not used on farms until the early twentieth century.

10
00:00:47.465 --> 00:00:53.907
More than 6,000 years ago, people began to cultivate vegetables and grains in the Fertile Crescent, the area

11
00:00:53.947 --> 00:00:56.368
in the Middle East where civilization first developed.

12
00:00:57.212 --> 00:01:02.035
Over time, they discovered that if they added human or animal dung to the soil, their crops would

13
00:01:02.075 --> 00:01:03.116
produce higher yields.

14
00:01:03.937 --> 00:01:09.320
Meanwhile, in China, farmers kept ducks and fish in their rice fields to eat weeds and help fertilize

15
00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:10.101
the rice plants.

16
00:01:10.661 --> 00:01:14.344
These methods were used until the twentieth century all over the world.

17
00:01:15.324 --> 00:01:22.929
The Green Revolution After World War II, agriculture underwent a massive change, which the media called the Green

18
00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:32.398
Revolution. Irrigation technology was greatly improved, new farm machinery became commonplace, and scientists introduced hybrid crops that could

19
00:01:32.438 --> 00:01:33.639
grow better and faster.

20
00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:39.862
Farmers also began to use artificial fertilizers and pesticides to help them improve yields.

21
00:01:40.502 --> 00:01:45.864
This trend initially started in the United States, where chemical companies turned their attention to growing food to

22
00:01:45.904 --> 00:01:48.205
deal with rising demand from the growing population.

23
00:01:49.126 --> 00:01:54.428
To do this, scientists studied what kinds of chemicals plants require for robust growth.

24
00:01:55.084 --> 00:02:00.127
They discovered that most of these could be produced synthetically and applied to the fields to boost the

25
00:02:00.187 --> 00:02:01.168
quality of the soil.

26
00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:08.412
Nitrogen, for example, is essential for the survival of a plant and can be created artificially and sprayed

27
00:02:08.452 --> 00:02:09.873
onto the soil as a liquid.

28
00:02:10.673 --> 00:02:14.795
Other nutrients essential to plants can be applied in a variety of methods as well.

29
00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:22.600
As the crops grow, they are vulnerable to many pests, such as bacteria, insects, rodents, and other animals.

30
00:02:23.264 --> 00:02:29.228
Chemical companies also hoped to create pesticides that would reduce the threat from these pests, allowing the crops

31
00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:29.788
to mature.

32
00:02:29.808 --> 00:02:39.254
A breakthrough occurred in 1939; Swiss chemist Paul Müller found that a chemical compound called DDT was able

33
00:02:39.314 --> 00:02:40.834
to kill insects easily.

34
00:02:41.555 --> 00:02:45.837
Around the world, chemical companies began selling it to farmers in great quantities.

35
00:02:46.658 --> 00:02:53.141
By 1945, most farms in the United States and Great Britain were relying on the chemical to protect

36
00:02:53.181 --> 00:02:56.262
their crops from insects and ensure high yields.

37
00:02:57.022 --> 00:03:03.083
The benefits were undeniable; farmers were able to grow more food to feed the world's population, which was

38
00:03:03.143 --> 00:03:04.244
increasing rapidly.

39
00:03:04.904 --> 00:03:10.365
The Green Revolution prevented the starvation of billions of people who would not otherwise have had enough food

40
00:03:10.405 --> 00:03:10.746
to eat.

41
00:03:11.946 --> 00:03:19.128
After the Green Revolution By the 1960s, people began to notice certain negative side effects caused by these

42
00:03:19.168 --> 00:03:25.655
techniques. Although the Green Revolution allowed farmers to keep pace with population growth, it did so at the

43
00:03:25.715 --> 00:03:30.698
expense of the environment, safety to humans, and the overall quality of food.

44
00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:38.403
The organic movement gained popularity when it was reported that the widespread use of artificial fertilizers and pesticides

45
00:03:38.743 --> 00:03:40.104
was damaging the environment.

46
00:03:40.805 --> 00:03:45.908
Water quality deteriorates when farmers overuse artificial fertilizers and pesticides.

47
00:03:46.656 --> 00:03:52.959
This is because the excess chemicals leak through the soil into the underground water system or are flushed

48
00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:54.919
into nearby ponds and creeks.

49
00:03:55.660 --> 00:04:01.082
This leads to high levels of nitrogen, potassium, and other chemicals that are poisonous to living creatures in

50
00:04:01.102 --> 00:04:02.282
nearby bodies of water.

51
00:04:03.163 --> 00:04:06.904
Animals that live in these water sources or get their food from them suffer.

52
00:04:07.825 --> 00:04:13.807
For example, the concentration of DDT ingested by bald eagles through the fish they eat prevents them from

53
00:04:13.867 --> 00:04:14.807
laying healthy eggs.

54
00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:22.742
So, in the 1950s and 1960s, the eggs would hatch before their time, and the hatchlings died, causing

55
00:04:22.782 --> 00:04:25.923
a serious drop in the bald eagle population in the U.S.

56
00:04:26.963 --> 00:04:32.125
It was also suggested that the use of artificial chemicals was related to certain problems with human health.

57
00:04:32.865 --> 00:04:38.146
People exposed to high levels of pesticides, such as the farmers who apply them, have higher rates of

58
00:04:38.206 --> 00:04:44.248
cancer and birth defects as well as more problems with their respiratory systems, skin, and memory.

59
00:04:44.972 --> 00:04:51.395
But it is possible to be exposed to these chemicals outside of the fields; chemical residues often remain

60
00:04:51.495 --> 00:04:56.057
on the fruit and vegetables bought in stores, posing health concerns for people.

61
00:04:56.897 --> 00:04:58.178
One study done in the U.S.

62
00:04:58.218 --> 00:05:03.960
showed that over 70% of the fruit found in stores contains at least one type of pesticide, and

63
00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.561
sometimes as many as forty.

64
00:05:06.281 --> 00:05:11.484
Consumers have also noted that the quality and taste of foods grown with artificial chemicals have changed for

65
00:05:11.524 --> 00:05:11.944
the worse.

66
00:05:12.784 --> 00:05:15.745
A good-looking product appeals to consumers in the supermarket.

67
00:05:16.326 --> 00:05:21.908
Tomatoes, for instance, are grown to have a thick skin so they don't bruise easily when in transport

68
00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:22.588
or storage.

69
00:05:23.208 --> 00:05:26.750
Unfortunately, this has the side effect of diminishing the tomatoes' flavor.

70
00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:34.173
Furthermore, crops grown with artificial chemicals have a lower nutritional content because most fertilizers are made of only

71
00:05:34.213 --> 00:05:35.493
a few key compounds.

72
00:05:36.134 --> 00:05:41.256
As a result, the plants contain far fewer of the many minerals and vitamins that humans need in

73
00:05:41.276 --> 00:05:41.856
their diets.

74
00:05:42.604 --> 00:05:46.926
For example, tomatoes that are not organically grown are much lower in Vitamin C.

75
00:05:47.766 --> 00:05:53.329
The Organic Foods Trend With so many reasons to avoid fruits and vegetables that are grown with artificial

76
00:05:53.369 --> 00:05:57.430
chemicals, it is no wonder that people have started buying organic foods.

77
00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:03.093
But how can farmers grow enough food for billions of people and not rely on artificial fertilizers and

78
00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:10.015
pesticides? Organic farmers understand that healthy plants need healthy soil, so they concentrate on making sure the soil

79
00:06:10.055 --> 00:06:11.036
gets enough nutrients.

80
00:06:11.844 --> 00:06:17.106
One way to do this is to follow the example of ancient farmers by making a natural fertilizer

81
00:06:17.426 --> 00:06:20.807
out of compost, a mixture of decomposing vegetable matter.

82
00:06:21.607 --> 00:06:27.088
Farmers can easily make compost by collecting the stems and other leftover parts of plants that are not

83
00:06:27.228 --> 00:06:27.908
used for food.

84
00:06:28.629 --> 00:06:33.650
Then, they put this plant material into a container where it can rot until it is ready to

85
00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:34.190
be used.

86
00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:40.848
Using compost provides essential nutrients for the fields and uses up all the waste from the crops, a

87
00:06:40.888 --> 00:06:41.809
type of recycling.

88
00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:48.334
Farmers can also use compost as mulch, which is a layer of material that is spread on top

89
00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:48.995
of the soil.

90
00:06:49.856 --> 00:06:56.381
Mulch made from grass clippings, straw, or bark chips can provide moisture for soil in dry climates and

91
00:06:56.441 --> 00:06:58.563
protect the fields from wind erosion.

92
00:06:59.383 --> 00:07:06.409
Most importantly, farmers must give soil enough time between harvests to regain its nutritional content and strength.

93
00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:12.302
If they can't let their fields lie unused and rest, they can practice crop rotation.

94
00:07:13.023 --> 00:07:18.387
Farmers who rotate their crops alternate which plants they grow on the same land, as opposed to growing

95
00:07:18.427 --> 00:07:23.552
the same crop in the same place season after season, which eventually depletes the soil's nutrients.

96
00:07:24.173 --> 00:07:29.718
Barley, for instance, requires a lot of nitrogen, but beans can replace nitrogen in the soil.

97
00:07:30.418 --> 00:07:36.464
If farmers alternate between barley and beans on the same field, they can maintain balanced and healthy soil.

98
00:07:37.328 --> 00:07:42.050
Of course, using organic methods is not as easy as spraying a field with artificial chemicals.

99
00:07:42.731 --> 00:07:49.073
It's a time-consuming and expensive process, and farmers must be knowledgeable about how to manage their crops using

100
00:07:49.134 --> 00:07:49.974
organic methods.

101
00:07:50.714 --> 00:07:55.056
Consequently, organic foods tend to be more expensive than nonorganic foods.

102
00:07:55.636 --> 00:08:00.819
For many people, this is a reasonable price to pay for healthy produce that tastes great and is

103
00:08:00.859 --> 00:08:03.120
good for the environment and the people in it.
